1
00:00:00,062 --> 00:00:02,492
(Penny:)Hey, if you're pausing
for dramatic effect,

2
00:00:02,497 --> 00:00:04,897
(Penny:)I'd keep it moving.

3
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:06,130
(Leonard:)No, no.

4
00:00:08,503 --> 00:00:11,743
(Leonard:)People don't talk
about surface tension.

5
00:00:11,740 --> 00:00:15,180
(Leonard:)If you imagine our
three-space as the surface

6
00:00:15,177 --> 00:00:17,747
(Leonard:)of an N-dimensional
superfluid bubble...

7
00:00:17,746 --> 00:00:20,876
(Leonard:)This... is exciting.

8
00:00:20,882 --> 00:00:22,252
(Leonard:)This is really exciting.

9
00:00:22,250 --> 00:00:23,420
(Leonard:)I have to go
find Sheldon.

10
00:00:23,418 --> 00:00:26,418
(Leonard:)Okay, well,
if you find him,

11
00:00:26,421 --> 00:00:27,851
(Penny:)use the kitchen island--

12
00:00:27,856 --> 00:00:29,486
(Penny:)that coffee table will not
support both of you.

13
00:00:32,727 --> 00:00:35,467
(Leonard:)Which means a spherical
multidimensional superfluid

14
00:00:35,464 --> 00:00:37,894
(Leonard:)shows the same negative-energy
density as space-time.

15
00:00:37,899 --> 00:00:40,429
(Leonard:)So what do you think? What do
you think? So what do you think?

16
00:00:43,805 --> 00:00:45,805
(Sheldon:)Hmm...

17
00:00:45,807 --> 00:00:47,277
(Leonard:)What? Is it wrong?

18
00:00:47,275 --> 00:00:48,775
(Leonard:)Have you seen it somewhere else?

19
00:00:51,079 --> 00:00:53,149
(Sheldon:)Hmm...

20
00:00:54,116 --> 00:00:55,546
(Leonard:)I know this isn't my area,

21
00:00:55,550 --> 00:00:57,620
(Leonard:)and I could never
do the math like you can,

22
00:00:57,619 --> 00:00:59,289
(Leonard:)but could this be something...?

23
00:00:59,287 --> 00:01:00,387
(Leonard:)Well...

